OL,3,AMillions urged to evacuate as powerful
OL,4,ATyphoon Dujuan hits Japan
OL,5,
OL,6,FAlmost two million people are under
OL,7,Fevacuation orders in Japan as Typhoon
OL,8,FDujuan batters a number of the
OL,9,Fcountry's prefectures.
OL,11,FJapan's Meteorological Agency had
OL,12,Fwarned of an "imminent threat to life",
OL,13,Fbut several warnings have now been
OL,14,Fdowngraded, with the danger to life
OL,15,Fwarning remaining in place in Oshima
OL,16,FTown.
OL,18,FThe country's public broadcaster, NHK,
OL,19,Freported that two people had died and
OL,20,Ffour others were missing as a result of
OL,21,Fthe typhoon. It also reported four were
OL,22,Fmissing in Kanagawa prefecture.
OL,23,APub: 21-SepQpppppppppppppppppppppG13/39
